# The minimized corpus is checked in. See SPEC.md §21.3 for why: a CI smoke that
# starts from nothing spends its budget rediscovering each format, and the packet
# targets reached only 29 and 24 inputs that way.
#
# `cargo fuzz run` writes new inputs here. Those are additions, not rewrites, so a
# working tree can be dirty after a campaign; the committed set is the cmin output
# plus the reproducer for every fixed crash.
#
# The set is large on disk (19MB) and small in the repository (~580KB), because git
# stores the gzipped form. The original "not checked in: they are large" reasoning
# applied to the first number and not the second.
